  "final_report": "[stop_reason: hop_cap_reached | hops used: 4/4]\n\nAnalyst summary:\n**Investigation goal** \u2013 Identify the companies that are structurally \u201cdown\u2011stream\u201d from Dow (i.e., customers or alternative suppliers) and determine whether any of them show documentary evidence of being affected by the disruption first reported on\u202f25\u202fAugust\u202f2017.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Structural exposure (down\u2011stream tiers)\n\nThe **traverse_supply_graph** call (mode\u202f=\u202f\u201cdownstream\u201d, max_tier\u202f=\u202f2) returned a ranked list of companies that are most likely to be impacted by a disruption at Dow.  \n\n| Tier | Companies (high\u2011confidence / medium\u2011confidence) |\n|------|-------------------------------------------------|\n| **Tier\u202f1** (direct downstream) | Toray Industries, Formosa Plastics, Saudi Arabian Oil, Hyundai Motor, Samsung Electronics, Avient, HDC Hyundai Engineering Plastics, etc. |\n| **Tier\u202f2** (one step further) | Renault, Ford Motor, Toyota Motor, Volkswagen, Mercedes\u2011Benz, Aptiv, LG Energy Solution, Panasonic, ZF TRW Automotive, Stellantis, Tesla, Bosch, etc. |\n\n(Full tier\u20111 and tier\u20112 lists are reproduced in the tool output above.)\n\nThese companies are therefore **structurally at risk** \u2013 they either buy chemicals, polymers or other intermediate products from Dow, or they could be alternative suppliers for downstream users of those materials.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Evidence search\n\nTwo evidence sources were consulted:\n\n| Tool | Query / Target | Result |\n|------|----------------|--------|\n| **get_supplier_info** (company\u2011specific filing) | *Hyundai Motor* (representative Tier\u202f1 company) \u2013 event date 2017\u201108\u201125 | No filings on record for \u201cHyundai Motor\u201d in the database. |\n| **search_corpus** (free\u2011text across all filings) | `\"Dow disruption\"` with event date\u202f=\u202f2017\u201108\u201125 (unfiltered) | Returned 20 hits, none of which mention Dow in connection with a supply\u2011chain disruption on that date. The matches were unrelated (e.g., BP risk language, generic crisis\u2011management text, other companies\u2019 disclosures). No specific reference to Dow, nor to any of the downstream firms listed above, could be located. |\n\nBecause **search_corpus** was run without a company filter (the purpose was to discover whether any filing mentioned the Dow event at all), the returned documents do not provide confirmation that any of the identified downstream companies experienced an impact.\n\n---\n\n### 3. What could NOT be confirmed\n\n| Company | Structural link to Dow | Documentary evidence of impact on\u202f25\u2011Aug\u20112017 disruption |\n|---------|------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|\n| Toray Industries | Tier\u202f1 \u2013 buyer of carbon\u2011fiber composites & engineering resins from Dow | **No** mention found in filings or corpus. |\n| Formosa Plastics | Tier\u202f1 \u2013 PVC & epoxy resin customer | **No** evidence located. |\n| Saudi Arabian Oil | Tier\u202f1 \u2013 crude oil/petroleum product consumer (indirect) | **No** evidence located. |\n| Hyundai Motor | Tier\u202f1 \u2013 automotive OEM, high\u2011confidence downstream | **No filing found**; no corpus mention. |\n| Samsung Electronics | Tier\u202f1 \u2013 automotive electronics supplier | **No** evidence located. |\n| Avient | Tier\u202f1 \u2013 specialty polymer compounds buyer | **No** evidence located. |\n| (All other Tier\u202f1 & Tier\u202f2 firms) | Structural exposure per graph | **No** specific filing or corpus reference to a Dow\u2011related disruption on the target date. |\n\nIn short, while the supply\u2011graph clearly shows many companies that could be affected by a problem at Dow, **the document set available through `get_supplier_info` and `search_corpus` does not contain any explicit statements that these firms experienced a disruption linked to Dow in late\u202fAugust\u202f2017**.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Summary judgment\n\n* **Structural risk:** Dozens of downstream manufacturers and suppliers (automakers, chemical processors, oil & gas producers, battery makers, etc.) are theoretically exposed to a supply interruption at Dow.\n* **Evidence status:** No concrete SEC\u2011filing language or corpus excerpt was found that confirms any of these companies reported an impact from the specific 25\u202fAug\u202f2017 Dow disruption. The only filing\u2011level check attempted (Hyundai Motor) returned no record, and the broad \u201cDow disruption\u201d search produced unrelated material.\n* **Conclusion:** Based on the data available within the tool budget, we cannot verify that any downstream company publicly disclosed being affected by the Dow event of 25\u202fAugust\u202f2017. The list of structurally\u2011at\u2011risk firms is therefore **informational only**; further investigation would require access to additional sources (e.g., news archives, press releases, or more recent SEC filings) beyond what was provided here.\n\nCOVERAGE GAPS (74) -- reported explicitly, not omitted:\n  - toray industries: no evidence gathered\n  - nan ya plastics: no evidence gathered\n  - formosa plastics: no evidence gathered\n  - saudi arabian oil: no evidence gathered\n  - grupo pochteca sab de cv: no evidence gathered\n  - hyundai motor: no evidence gathered\n  - samsung electronics: no evidence gathered\n  - hdc hyundai engineering plastics: no evidence gathered\n  - renault: no evidence gathered\n  - posco international: no evidence gathered\n  - toyota tsusho: no evidence gathered\n  - china petroleum & chemical: no evidence gathered\n  - alfa sab de cv: no evidence gathered\n  - nexteer automotive: no evidence gathered\n  - ford motor: no evidence gathered\n  - arcelormittal: no evidence gathered\n  - shun on electronic: no evidence gathered\n  - baic bluepark new energy technology: no evidence gathered\n  - formosa petrochemical: n